{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart","id":880508,"title":"Compare and Contrast Pentex With Buffyverses \"Wolfram and Hart\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-02T15:06:13-07:00","id":880508,"title":"Compare and Contrast Pentex With Buffyverses \"Wolfram and Hart\"","content":"Am I the only Person who see's these two fictional corporations as very similar.<br /> <br /> Both are EVIL thats obvious.<br /> <br /> both are sworn to Evil overlordly masters<br /> <br /> Both are believers in <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EqualOpportunityEvil\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...pportunityEvil</a><br /> <br /> With remarkably diverse sets of employees and brass.<br /> <br /> As well as cutting edge tech, as well as magic and psychics to launch investigations and such.<br /> <br /> any ideas how the two groups are dissimilar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:32:35-07:00","id":880967,"title":"","content":"Well, the first and major point of divergence is that Pentex proper is a massive holding company that rarely interfaces directly with the world. Its name isn't front and centre, people don't go 'oh, Endron, that's Pentex right?' - they don't even think that anyone owns Endron unless they do some digging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:39:55-07:00","id":880970,"title":"","content":"Fair point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:36:04-07:00","id":881227,"title":"","content":"Wolfram and Hart does far more traditional supernatural stuff, they are demons who have a law firm that makes deals with people. I don't think there's a fast food division of WRH, or one that makes video games, or one that makes booze that gets you possessed by evil spirits. WRH seems something smaller that could easily exist within the greater Pentex framework.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:01:26-07:00","id":881282,"title":"","content":"was thinking of that actually... Its probaly what a Pentex Law Firm would look like could see pentex trying to gather info on unseelie fae, camarilla and sabbat as well as the mafia, and Nephandi Maybe even a shadow lord or two via a law firm...<br /> <br /> Oh a picture I had in my head is pentex trying to appropiate a caerns land on the ground of &quot;Iminent domain&quot; &quot;Our building a Factory here, will create Jobs, more people employed and more Taxes&quot;<br /> <br /> ideas how a garou or kin lawyer could contest that claim?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T19:34:08-07:00","id":881418,"title":"","content":"So to bring in a evil lawyer fun....what would be a good replacement name for the firm? As to avoid looking like a blatant knock off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T20:14:53-07:00","id":881439,"title":"","content":"Hey Freak legion had, &quot;Braney the purple dinosaur (actually a wyrm corrupted Mokole)&quot; <br /> <br /> to be fair, in spite of being autistic, and borderline MR in terms of my social skills I laughed at that.<br /> <br /> <br /> depends on our tolerance for camp...<br /> <br /> I'd prefer low tolerance myself<br /> <br /> So ideas, possibly named after its founder whoever that is, possibly a still existent vampire or living Ferectoi, who has a sterling reputation<br /> <br /> And hmmmn another question would this evil law firm,all but boast &quot;We Sell the right to commit murder&quot; like W&amp;H did, or try to look a tad more ethical.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T20:33:35-07:00","id":881446,"title":"","content":"How &quot;Awake&quot; are they as a law firm are they? A straight port of WRH would be a reasonable intermediary for selling your soul to other demons, but also might be the sort of people you might go to if you are blood hunted and want it fixed. Which makes it weird on the Masquerade front.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it a supernatural law firm that is purely neutral might be more interesting than a wyrmfirm..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:15:19-07:00","id":881475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=881227#post881227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolfram and Hart does far more traditional supernatural stuff, they are demons who have a law firm that makes deals with people. I don't think there's a fast food division of WRH, or one that makes video games, or one that makes booze that gets you possessed by evil spirits. WRH seems something smaller that could easily exist within the greater Pentex framework.</div> </div> </div> </div>The commonalities between Pentex and WRH come, pretty bluntly, from touching <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EvilInc\" target=\"_blank\">similar</a> base <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/NebulousEvilOrganisation\" target=\"_blank\">tropes</a> with a supernatural note for a twist - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Devil&#39;s_Advocate_%281997_film%29\" target=\"_blank\">far</a> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/NextWorld\" target=\"_blank\">from</a> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Cheiron_Group\" target=\"_blank\">alone</a> in it, either.<br /> <br /> Personally, i don't really see something like Wolfram working as Pentex's legal arm, as the group is far more in collecting favors, influence and souls while keeping the world's status quo mostly the same than Pentex spiritual corruption/pollution/terraformation agenda.<br /> <br /> WRH's style seems far more reminiscent of kindred, demons, maybe changelings (admit i might be mixing up with CoD's changelings here) or a joint colaboration of sorts, at least to me, what's far from a problem, as i guess there's more than enough supernatural in the World of Darkness for other groups beside Pentex to exist with their own quite unrelated but equally weird agendas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=881418#post881418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to bring in a evil lawyer fun....what would be a good replacement name for the firm? As to avoid looking like a blatant knock off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in an &quot;Exalted Modern&quot; game i once conceived with a group of friends we came up with &quot;Wolfman &amp; *<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kid#Common_meanings\" target=\"_blank\">Kid</a>&quot;, possibly the opposite of &quot;not blatant&quot; but then my point was to make a sort of mash-up joke/antagonist, with &quot;Wolfman &amp; Kid&quot; as our twist of sorts on not only WRH but Apocalypse's Pentex and Forsaken's Pure, with Wolf, Man and Kid as nicknames of three lines of supernatural descendants of Exalted's Ma-ha-Suchi, a Lunar elder who's basically a bad-ass Crinos with some goat-like features/mutations<br /> <br /> Anyway, i would guess a name depends on what kind of imagery, idea or themes one wants.<br /> <br /> *kid, as the link is supposed to show, is also a common term for a young goat, in case some people are asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T00:23:39-07:00","id":881569,"title":"","content":"Oddly, despite the constant refrains about how law is banal, of the law firms with supernatural links in the oWoD one of the larger ones is owned by a Changeling. We also have the Pentex-controlled firm of Meyers, Feinstein and Hargrett and the NextWorld linked Riley, Taylor and Wendt. The Ventrue have a camarilla/clan law school in Luxembourg called the Academie, which could be rather interesting on the 'blood hunt' front someone raised above. The most WRH option is not a proper law firm, but a loose association of lawyers called... The Associates. All of them are infernalists and cultists who enjoy the challenge and thrill of negotiating contracts with demons. There are 12 of them.<br /> <br /> There may be others I've missed, but that's the lay of the land in specific law firms as far as I'm aware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:09:00-07:00","id":881647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=881569#post881569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly, despite the constant refrains about how law is banal, of the law firms with supernatural links in the oWoD one of the larger ones is owned by a Changeling. We also have the Pentex-controlled firm of Meyers, Feinstein and Hargrett and the NextWorld linked Riley, Taylor and Wendt. The Ventrue have a camarilla/clan law school in Luxembourg called the Academie, which could be rather interesting on the 'blood hunt' front someone raised above. The most WRH option is not a proper law firm, but a loose association of lawyers called... The Associates. All of them are infernalists and cultists who enjoy the challenge and thrill of negotiating contracts with demons. There are 12 of them.<br /> <br /> There may be others I've missed, but that's the lay of the land in specific law firms as far as I'm aware.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great info as i was aware of none of those beside NextWorld - that its from Orpheus, that is hooks notwithstanding is mostly its own 'verse, independent from WoD - in the loosest of terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:54:32-07:00","id":882349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=881647#post881647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great info as i was aware of none of those beside NextWorld - that its from Orpheus, that is hooks notwithstanding is mostly its own 'verse, independent from WoD - in the loosest of terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Orpheus was mostly separate, but Wr20 is going to have an appendix on it, so it can pretty much fit in as a part of Wraith from here on in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T19:34:56-07:00","id":882454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=881475#post881475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The commonalities between Pentex and WRH come, pretty bluntly, from touching <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EvilInc\" target=\"_blank\">similar</a> base <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/NebulousEvilOrganisation\" target=\"_blank\">tropes</a> with a supernatural note for a twist - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Devil&#39;s_Advocate_%281997_film%29\" target=\"_blank\">far</a> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/NextWorld\" target=\"_blank\">from</a> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Cheiron_Group\" target=\"_blank\">alone</a> in it, either.<br /> <br /> Personally, i don't really see something like Wolfram working as Pentex's legal arm, as the group is far more in collecting favors, influence and souls while keeping the world's status quo mostly the same than Pentex spiritual corruption/pollution/terraformation agenda.<br /> <br /> WRH's style seems far more reminiscent of kindred, demons, maybe changelings (admit i might be mixing up with CoD's changelings here) or a joint colaboration of sorts, at least to me, what's far from a problem, as i guess there's more than enough supernatural in the World of Darkness for other groups beside Pentex to exist with their own quite unrelated but equally weird agendas.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I Feel like WRH's style might actually work better in COD vs WOD. Still this is about having an evil law firm in your apocalypse chronicles so the last werebat can use his lawyering rather than just his vigilanting at night...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T20:18:20-07:00","id":882488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=882454#post882454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I Feel like WRH's style might actually work better in COD vs WOD. Still this is about having an evil law firm in your apocalypse chronicles so the last werebat can use his lawyering rather than just his vigilanting at night...</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, WoD is sometimes all too prone to inserting things in pre-existing packages/splats or certain &quot;global&quot; narratives instead of let them run on their own and at face value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T22:14:35-07:00","id":882561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=882488#post882488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly, WoD is sometimes all too prone to inserting things in pre-existing packages/splats or certain &quot;global&quot; narratives instead of let them run on their own and at face value.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its more the complete and utter genocidal balkanizaton of the supernatural community. A straight port of WRH feels like it should have its fingers in alot of pies.. but you can't say be a neutral go between say the Technocracy and the Sabbat. You could more readily do that in the East but they are a profoundly western feeling concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T01:13:22-07:00","id":882661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=882349#post882349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Orpheus was mostly separate, but Wr20 is going to have an appendix on it, so it can pretty much fit in as a part of Wraith from here on in.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, considering the format, layout and style of Orpheus... it always kinda felt like a prototype NWoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T04:08:19-07:00","id":882754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=882661#post882661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, considering the format, layout and style of Orpheus... it always kinda felt like a prototype NWoD game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can certainly be seen that way, or at least as an alternative look on the Revised Era with its closed narrative focus, though yes, it does concentrate more in people dealing with a mysterious world than being the monster/wizard as previous WoD titles.<br /> <br /> On a curious aside, i did use the Orpheus series as frame and inspiration in shaping a plot &amp; timeline of my own for an Aberrant chronicle a bunch of years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T20:18:13-07:00","id":886919,"title":"","content":"Wolfram and Hart could just as easily be adopted into a joint Fenrir and Fianna project. The totem spirits act as the patrons with kinfolk filling the majority of positions. This gives the Garou Nation a solid legal base to take on all manner of lawsuits. Particularly if you align Wolfram and Hart with a lobbying firm that is controlled by Shadow Lords and Children of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:26:55-07:00","id":887193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=886919#post886919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolfram and Hart could just as easily be adopted into a joint Fenrir and Fianna project. The totem spirits act as the patrons with kinfolk filling the majority of positions. This gives the Garou Nation a solid legal base to take on all manner of lawsuits. Particularly if you align Wolfram and Hart with a lobbying firm that is controlled by Shadow Lords and Children of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>A law firm could relate to a number of tribes, on its own or as allied fronts: Silver Fangs, Shadow Lords, Glass Walkers, Children of Gaia, Black Furies, basically any tribe - with the possible exceptions of Bone Gnawers or Red Talons - could make it work with only minimal backstory/excuses work, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:08:59-07:00","id":887226,"title":"","content":"Not sure Stargazers would be able to fit a law firm either...<br /> <br /> possibly not the wendigo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T13:52:33-07:00","id":887470,"title":"","content":"I'm certain any number of tribes could pull off a law firm like Wolfram and Hart. I chose Fenrir and Fianna simply for the name connection. There have been a number of posts on the forum about the Children of Gaia and the lack of substance as portrayed in official sources an effective lobbying firm controlled by the tribe would in my opinion be a step in the right direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:16:30-07:00","id":887485,"title":"","content":"curious something I asked somewhere else I didnt see an answer, idea of what a garou or kin lawyer, can say to an imminent domain claim on a septs lands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:33:34-07:00","id":887501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=887485#post887485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">curious something I asked somewhere else I didnt see an answer, idea of what a garou or kin lawyer, can say to an imminent domain claim on a septs lands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the situation and the area, currently in my state there is a pipeline that is being proposed. The survey company was caught on private land twice. The pipeline is being sold that only public land will be used. If suddenly this becomes seizing property to build the pipeline then the lawsuits will start. There is a property near me that was seized by imminent domain to expand a highway but in fact was going to be used as a massive roadstop and plaza. The court case is still happening as the state wants to sell the land to a developer. A developer that could not buy the land as it was part of a farm heritage trust. Imminent domain laws generally have to have a clear purpose: building a road, revitalizing a blighted area, or serving the public interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:50:39-07:00","id":887688,"title":"","content":"hmmmn say &quot;We want to clear this old park, so we can build a new factory, creating new jobs and revitalizing the economy&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:26:04-07:00","id":887715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=887688#post887688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmn say &amp;quot;We want to clear this old park, so we can build a new factory, creating new jobs and revitalizing the economy&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No need for imminent domain the government just needs to approve the sale of the land and possibly rezone. Possibly having a new park being donated by the corporation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:27:45-07:00","id":887718,"title":"","content":"An imminent domain case would be more along the lines of this private camp/property is sitting on prime real estate for a housing development or pipeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:46:16-07:00","id":887729,"title":"","content":"Bone Gnawer and kin lawyers seem pretty likely to me, in response to Baaldam. The urban poor produce a surprising number of lawyers world-wide, and while the upper levels of law are still skewed towards the wealthy, about half of lawyers are from lower socio-economic backgrounds. This is especially the case with two areas of particular interest to the Garou: Petty crime stuff, and environmental law, neither of which tend to attract as many bigshot wealthy lawyers as they aren't where the money is.<br /> <br /> Well, unless you're an environmental lawyer for a big firm, but that's more 'defending the corporate scum from environmental cases'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:12:44-07:00","id":887977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=887226#post887226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure Stargazers would be able to fit a law firm either...<br /> <br /> possibly not the wendigo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? A Stargazer would probably be the beast speaker able to bend minds and change any jury's (or judge's) mind to his point of view. And I'm pretty sure all native communities need a good lawyer to cover the White Man encroaching on their territory and taking their rights, running their casinos and building class action suits against the government for the poor living conditions of the reservations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T05:08:09-07:00","id":888074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=887977#post887977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? A Stargazer would probably be the beast speaker able to bend minds and change any jury's (or judge's) mind to his point of view. And I'm pretty sure all native communities need a good lawyer to cover the White Man encroaching on their territory and taking their rights, running their casinos and building class action suits against the government for the poor living conditions of the reservations.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, the philosophical bent of the Stargazers could actually fit pretty well with a university professor at law for example and in relation to Uktena &amp; Wendigo, there has been stuff going up between some native american reserves and federal government that seems to imply quite well that many of them have actually worked pretty hard in setting up good law counseling for themselves in the last half century, possibly making them the tribes with most the &quot;community backstory&quot; for such a setup beside possibly the Glass Walkers or Children of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:25:48-07:00","id":888167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/880508-compare-and-contrast-pentex-with-buffyverses-wolfram-and-hart?p=887718#post887718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An imminent domain case would be more along the lines of this private camp/property is sitting on prime real estate for a housing development or pipeline.</div> </div> </di